Smoke test: Investigate this SPECIFIC candidate set of USA/Canada-adjacent multiday group travel / experiential program employers for on-trip GROUP LEADER hiring signals. The core target is multiday group travel leadership, not only rugged outdoor instruction. Look for field instructor, program leader, trip leader, tour leader, trip manager, travel director, or guide roles. Do not do broad discovery first. ## Regions United States and Canada only. ## Must match - Multiday programs with overnight travel - Lead/facilitate a student or young-adult group (gap year, summer, study abroad OK) - Outdoor/adventure/service/cultural immersion focus preferred; broader multiday educational or small-group travel leadership also relevant ## DO NOT USE indeed.com, linkedin.com/jobs, ziprecruiter.com, glassdoor.com, monster.com. Skip all generic aggregators. ## Candidate set — batch 3 (inspect these first) - Rustic Pathways — https://rusticpathways.com/ - Broadreach — https://www.gobroadreach.com/ - NOLS — https://www.nols.edu/ - Outward Bound — https://www.outwardbound.org/ - Overland Summers — https://overlandsummers.com/ - Apogee Adventures — https://www.apogeeadventures.com/ - Deer Hill Expeditions — https://deerhillexpeditions.com/ - Pacific Discovery — https://www.pacificdiscovery.org/ - Where There Be Dragons — https://www.wheretherebedragons.com/ - Camp Leaders — https://www.campleaders.com/ ## Strict visit budget - **ONE URL per visit tool call.** Never batch multiple companies in a single visit. - Visit at most 10 pages total. - Careers/work-with-us/join-our-team pages first for each candidate. - If blocked, record watchlist and move on. - After 8 visits OR 6 companies with any signal, STOP and write the final answer. ## Output Use whatever format is natural and compact. For each useful employer or watchlist candidate, include company, country, role title(s), careers URL, program length, audience, hiring signal, and fit. Aim for 5–8 useful candidates. Preserve watchlist entries when multiday programs are clear but postings are absent. 
